1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:02,220
Hi, I'm Rafad Abdul Rasheed.

2
00:00:02,980 --> 00:00:04,420
When a company brings on a supplier,

3
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,620
someone has to bring together the
application,

4
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:08,720
supporting documents and follow-up
questions.

5
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:10,880
A missing detail can delay a good
supplier.

6
00:00:11,540 --> 00:00:13,940
A missed mismatch can create risk.

7
00:00:14,860 --> 00:00:18,420
Zamp keeps the information, checks and
next steps together,

8
00:00:18,920 --> 00:00:21,180
so suppliers know what to do and reviewers
can

9
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:22,760
see why a case needs a change.

10
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:26,280
The profiles here are fictional, and Zoya
at the

11
00:00:26,280 --> 00:00:29,100
bottom works in procurement at another
buyer company.

12
00:00:29,420 --> 00:00:31,020
Her cases stay separate from Apex.

13
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:36,580
I'll start as Vikram using the supplier
profile linked

14
00:00:36,580 --> 00:00:38,240
to his company, Apex Components.

15
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:43,000
First, I confirm the business name, type
and address.

16
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:46,840
This application belongs to Apex
Components, so its documents

17
00:00:46,840 --> 00:00:48,780
and decisions stay with the right
supplier.

18
00:00:50,360 --> 00:00:52,000
Next are the tax details.

19
00:00:53,020 --> 00:00:56,700
Zamp checks the format here, then compares
the entered values

20
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:58,700
with what it reads from supporting
documents.

21
00:00:58,980 --> 00:01:01,620
Registry responses in this demo are
simulated.

22
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:05,940
Here, the buyer gets a named person for
questions

23
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:06,780
and follow-up.

24
00:01:10,790 --> 00:01:15,270
Bank details can be checked against the
uploaded proof.

25
00:01:16,010 --> 00:01:18,970
Sensitive account numbers are masked in
staff views.

26
00:01:19,970 --> 00:01:24,570
Business activity helps the buyer decide
which documents this

27
00:01:24,570 --> 00:01:25,710
supplier needs to provide.

28
00:01:26,410 --> 00:01:29,200
The checklist reflects this supplier's
business.

29
00:01:29,910 --> 00:01:33,710
Vikram can preview each file and see what
Zamp reads before

30
00:01:33,710 --> 00:01:34,260
submitting.

31
00:01:34,770 --> 00:01:38,490
OCR or text recognition is how Zamp reads
the

32
00:01:38,490 --> 00:01:39,040
document.

33
00:01:39,190 --> 00:01:41,310
Here it misread a character on the PAN
card.

34
00:01:41,830 --> 00:01:44,270
Vikram checks the preview, corrects the
value himself and

35
00:01:44,270 --> 00:01:44,950
explains why.

36
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:46,500
Both versions stay on record,

37
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:48,120
and checks run again.

38
00:01:48,130 --> 00:01:49,950
A reviewer still decides.

39
00:01:52,720 --> 00:01:56,160
Before sending the application Vikram
reviews it and makes

40
00:01:56,160 --> 00:01:57,540
the required declarations.

41
00:02:00,170 --> 00:02:02,450
Once submitted, Zamp runs the checks.

42
00:02:02,450 --> 00:02:05,290
and gives the supplier a reference and
status.

43
00:02:05,870 --> 00:02:07,710
Those checks highlight what needs
attention.

44
00:02:08,430 --> 00:02:10,630
They don't approve the application.

45
00:02:13,660 --> 00:02:16,180
Now I switch to Pooja's procurement
profile.

46
00:02:16,820 --> 00:02:18,560
She assigns the submitted case to Rajesh,

47
00:02:19,440 --> 00:02:21,760
so one reviewer owns the next step and the

48
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:22,460
handoff is recorded.

49
00:02:25,690 --> 00:02:28,070
Rajesh signs into his assigned queue.

50
00:02:28,550 --> 00:02:32,250
He opens the application and checks the
documents alongside

51
00:02:32,250 --> 00:02:33,650
the validation findings.

52
00:02:34,170 --> 00:02:36,650
This brings the evidence together for his
review.

53
00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:46,430
After reviewing the evidence and
confirming it supports

54
00:02:46,430 --> 00:02:48,000
approval, Rajesh records his decision.

55
00:02:48,560 --> 00:02:50,700
A person makes the final call.

56
00:02:53,100 --> 00:02:55,620
Vikram signs back in and sees the approval
notice,

57
00:02:56,060 --> 00:03:00,600
it confirms onboarding is complete and
tells him there

58
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:02,620
are no more tasks for this application.

59
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:07,520
Now, a different supplier submits a
separate case.

60
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:10,920
Zamp compares the PAN entered on the
application with

61
00:03:10,920 --> 00:03:12,660
the PAN encoded in the GSTIN.

62
00:03:13,380 --> 00:03:17,960
Characters 3 through 12 of a GSTIN are the

63
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:18,510
PAN.

64
00:03:18,520 --> 00:03:21,340
These values don't match, so approval is
held and

65
00:03:21,340 --> 00:03:23,260
the supplier is asked to check the right
entity's

66
00:03:23,260 --> 00:03:23,810
details.

67
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:24,920
This is synthetic data.

68
00:03:26,380 --> 00:03:28,350
The supplier checks the GST certificate,

69
00:03:28,950 --> 00:03:31,540
then enters the corrected GSTIN and
explains the change.

70
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:35,460
The response stays with the original
clarification for Rajesh

71
00:03:35,460 --> 00:03:36,010
to review.

72
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:38,240
Sending a reply moves the case forward.

73
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:39,400
It doesn't approve it.

74
00:03:45,590 --> 00:03:48,790
Rajesh sees the supplier's response on the
case and

75
00:03:48,790 --> 00:03:50,910
can review the change against the
evidence.

76
00:03:51,410 --> 00:03:53,510
He still decides whether the issue is
resolved.

77
00:04:03,620 --> 00:04:07,180
Here we can reopen the check and see why

78
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:08,120
approval was held.

79
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:10,940
That gives the team a clear reason to
refer

80
00:04:10,940 --> 00:04:12,600
to during review.

81
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:17,720
A simulated registry times out.

82
00:04:18,140 --> 00:04:21,120
That's unknown, not a supplier failure.

83
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:25,540
Staff can retry without asking the
supplier to resubmit.

84
00:04:27,170 --> 00:04:30,550
Across this flow, suppliers can see what
to provide

85
00:04:30,550 --> 00:04:31,410
and what needs attention.

86
00:04:32,070 --> 00:04:35,530
Procurement can assign ownership, and
reviewers can see the

87
00:04:35,530 --> 00:04:36,530
evidence behind the decision.

88
00:04:37,150 --> 00:04:40,090
Zamp flags, conflicts and routes,
questions to the right

89
00:04:40,090 --> 00:04:40,640
person.

90
00:04:40,950 --> 00:04:43,450
The documents and registry responses here
are synthetic.

91
00:04:43,930 --> 00:04:47,210
In a pilot, we track time to decision,
avoidable

92
00:04:47,210 --> 00:04:50,450
follow-ups, unsafe approvals and valid
suppliers held by

93
00:04:50,450 --> 00:04:51,000
mistake.

94
00:04:51,330 --> 00:04:52,050
Thank you for your time.

95
00:04:52,330 --> 00:04:56,450
I'm Rafad and this was our Zamp vendor
onboarding

96
00:04:56,450 --> 00:04:57,090
walkthrough.
